cff-version: 1.2.0
title: 'eessi-arch-guard: a Slurm TaskProlog for EESSI CPU and GPU target mismatches'
message: If you use eessi-arch-guard, please cite it using the metadata below.
type: software
authors:
- given-names: Rohit
  family-names: Goswami
  email: rgoswami@ieee.org
  orcid: https://orcid.org/0000-0002-2393-8056
license: MIT
repository-code: https://github.com/stackhands/eessi-arch-guard
url: https://stackhands.github.io/eessi-arch-guard/
keywords:
- EESSI
- Slurm
- Lmod
- CPU architecture
- HPC
abstract: Slurm TaskProlog that detects a CPU or GPU target mismatch between a task
  and its inherited EESSI module stack, reloads the stack through Lmod on the compute
  node and prints the environment delta, plus a pre-submit check, Lmod site hooks
  and mount checks.
